            The number to ask a dealer for is PTO horsepower, not engine horsepower. A 25 HP engine typically delivers 18 to 20 HP at the PTO, and implements are rated against that figure. A 5-foot rotary cutter specified for 20 PTO horsepower will disappoint on a machine delivering 16.
