              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How many acres do you need to justify a tractor?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Roughly two to three acres is the practical floor, and even then only if you regularly move material — gravel, mulch, soil, firewood, snow. Under that, a zero turn mower plus occasional equipment rental costs far less and does the job better. The loader, not the mower deck, is what actually justifies the purchase.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Sub-compact or compact tractor: which should I buy?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Buy sub-compact if your work is loader-led and the machine has to cross a maintained lawn. Buy compact if your work is implement-led — box blade, rotary cutter, tiller — because weight rather than horsepower is what keeps ground-engaging implements in the dirt. A compact tractor weighs roughly twice as much at similar rated horsepower.
              </p>
            </div>

